{"name":"Wild Hemp","hex":"#9d7b74","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"hemp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall annual herb, Cannabis sativa, native to Asia.","Various products of this plant, including fibres and the drug cannabis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hemp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Feral cannabis","blocks":[{"text":"Feral cannabis, or wild marijuana, is wild-growing cannabis generally descended from industrial hemp plants previously cultivated for fiber, with low or negligible amounts of psychoactive tetrahydrocannabinol (THC)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Marijuana%2C_Buffalo_County%2C_Nebraska%2C_2017-06-15.jpg/330px-Marijuana%2C_Buffalo_County%2C_Nebraska%2C_2017-06-15.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feral_cannabis"},{"title":"Hemp","blocks":[{"text":"The term hemp is the vernacular English language word designating the plant Cannabis sativa, a plant that can be used to make a wide range of products, and be refined into a variety of commercial items, including paper, rope, textiles, clothing, biodegradable plastics, paint, insulation, biofuel, food, medicines, and animal feed. Along with bamboo, hemp is among the fastest growing plants on Earth and was also one of the first plants to be spun into usable fiber 50,000 years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/La_Roche_J